 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Real-time performance is achieved by drawing the model once per shell. The number of ray tracing steps is minimized by using a 3D distance map to skip empty space [S1, abstract only].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Requires storage for the geometry volume texture and the 3D distance map [S1, abstract only]. This overcomes the high storage requirements of previous approaches like Wang et al. [S1, abstract only].
-*   **Strengths:** Handles arbitrary volumetric geometry and height-field shell geometry [S1, abstract only]. Reduces rendering artifacts for shallow view angles [S1, abstract only]. Overcomes mapping distortions and low shell geometry depth complexity found in Policarpo and Oliveira [S1, abstract only].
-*   **Limitations:** Silhouette gaps can be apparent if not remedied by fin textures or edge fading [S2, unofficial]. The method assumes a constant hair neighborhood for precomputed lighting, which may limit dynamic changes [S2, unofficial].
-*   **When to use:** When rendering complex microgeometry (like fur) in real-time with global lighting effects [S2, unofficial].
-*   **When not to use:** When dynamic changes to the microgeometry neighborhood are required that invalidate precomputed lighting [S2, unofficial].
+- **Time Complexity:** Optimized by the 3D distance map which skips empty space, minimizing ray tracing steps [S1, abstract only].
+- **Memory Complexity:** Uses a pre-computed tetrahedra mesh and 3D textures (volume texture and distance map) [S1, abstract only].
+- **Strengths:** Handles arbitrary volumetric geometry and height-field shell geometry; reduces artifacts at shallow view angles; includes local lighting [S1, abstract only].
+- **Limitations:** Requires pre-computation of the tetrahedra mesh and 3D textures [S1, abstract only].
+- **Comparison:** Overcomes high storage requirements and per-vertex computations of [Wang et al. 2004] and low shell geometry depth complexity and mapping distortions of [Policarpo and Oliveira 2006] [S1, abstract only].
 
 ## Background
-This technique was introduced to address shortcomings in previous shell space rendering approaches. Wang et al. [2004] had high storage requirements and involved per-vertex computations, while Policarpo and Oliveira [2006] suffered from low shell geometry depth complexity and mapping distortions [S1, abstract only]. The method builds on the shell idea for volume rendering [10496-shell-method-for-volume-rendering.md] and combines it with techniques for rendering microgeometry using precomputed radiance transfer (PRT) [S2, unofficial]. It is used for real-time rendering of fur and other complex surface details [S2, unofficial].
+This technique was introduced to address shortcomings in previous shell space rendering approaches [S1, abstract only]. It builds on the general shell idea but implements it via a tetrahedra-based volume definition and distance-map-accelerated ray tracing for real-time performance [S1, abstract only].
 
